Files: libhunmin/data/*
Copyright: 2026 Seo Bon Keun
           2009-2016 Choe Hwanjin and libhangul contributors
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later
 Comment: Generated (tools/kbd2data.py, tools/ist2data.py) from vendored
  libhangul 0.2.0 keyboard data under data-orig/ and from normative
  신세벌식 ist.xml sources; see tools/*.py headers for provenance.
  .
  This stanza is a DEFAULT for the directory. Three subdirectories carry their
  own terms and are staved separately below, because "Copyright: Seo Bon Keun
  / LGPL" over a ShareAlike derivative of a government dictionary was a false
  claim and would have shipped in every deb built from this file. Most specific
  stanza wins.

Files: libhunmin/data/hanja/*
Copyright: 2005-2006 Choe Hwanjin
License: BSD-3-Clause
 Comment: From libhangul-data 0.2.0-1build1, data/hanja/hanja.txt. The LGPL in
  libhangul's own copyright file covers the library, not this dictionary.
  Provenance in full: libhunmin/data/hanja/LICENSE.md.

Files: libhunmin/data/idioms/*
License: MIT
 Comment: Provenance in full: libhunmin/data/idioms/LICENSE.md.

Files: libhunmin/data/krdict/*
License: CC-BY-SA-2.0
 Comment: The jurisdiction the National Institute of Korean Language publishes
  under is the KR one, so the terms are CC-BY-SA 2.0 KR. Written as the bare
  SPDX identifier because CC-BY-SA-2.0-KR could not be validated as one from
  this host and an unrecognised licence name is worse than a coarser correct
  one -- check it before shipping and tighten if a KR identifier exists.
  .
  Derived from 국립국어원 한국어기초사전 (Korean Basic Dictionary),
  via the open-data dump spellcheck-ko/korean-dict-nikl. Only the extracted
  Hanja-bearing table is shipped; the 368 MB source dump is not vendored.
  Attribution required: "국립국어원 한국어기초사전".
  Provenance, the ShareAlike analysis and the upstream exclusions are in
  libhunmin/data/krdict/LICENSE.md.
  .
  PACKAGING GAP: the CC-BY-SA 2.0 KR text is NOT embedded below, and no copy
  exists under /usr/share/common-licenses on this host. A redistributable deb
  must ship the licence text for everything it redistributes, so this stanza
  names the licence and the attribution but does not by itself discharge that
  duty. Fetch the text and add it as a License: stanza before shipping.

